{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.physical_layer_leray","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.physical_layer_leray","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.low_mode_block_global","lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.surreal_enstrophy_finite_modes"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.multi_source_ladder_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.multi_source_ladder_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":1149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L1149-L1217","doc":"**All-pairs uniform suppression** (strong induction): with the\ngeometric all-pairs recurrence\n`β n ≤ (∑_{m<n} λ^{n−1−m}·β m²)/(ν·k n)` for `n ≥ 1`, a band\nbound `β 0 ≤ B`, and the all-pairs dissipation-scale condition\n`B ≤ θ·(1−λ)·ν·k n` (`θ ≤ 1`, `0 ≤ λ < 1`), every rung beyond\nthe band is uniformly `θ`-suppressed: `β n ≤ θ·B`.  The geometric\nweight sum is controlled by `∑_{j<n} λ^j ≤ 1/(1−λ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium_forced","kind":"theorem","line":1126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L1126-L1147","doc":"Per-rung equilibrium with arbitrary nonnegative constant forcing\n`Φ = kn·F`: a rung starting empty never exceeds `F/(ν·kn)`.\nGeneralizes `rung_equilibrium` (`F = P²`) and\n`rung_equilibrium_two_source` (`F = P₁² + γ·P₂²`); the SF9\nall-pairs geometric sum `F = ∑_{m<n} λ^{n−1−m}·P_m²` is the\nintended instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_two_source_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_two_source_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":1055,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L1055-L1105","doc":"**Trajectory-level two-source composition**: with every rung from\nthe third onward starting empty and satisfying the two-source\nper-amplitude DN step forced by the *actual trajectories* of the\ntwo rungs below, and the first two rungs uniformly bounded, every\nrung's whole trajectory obeys the two-term composed bound.  Pair\ninduction on rungs; each step is `rung_equilibrium_two_source`\nafter upgrading the trajectory forcing to its uniform bounds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rungBound2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rungBound2","kind":"def","line":1046,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L1046-L1053","doc":"The two-source composed per-rung bounds: boundary data `P₀, P₁`\non the first two rungs, then each rung at the two-source\nequilibrium forced by the previous two rungs' bounds. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.two_source_ladder_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.two_source_ladder_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":990,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L990-L1044","doc":"**Two-source ladder collapse** (pair-maximum induction): with the\ntwo-term recurrence `β(j+2) ≤ (β(j+1)² + γ·β j²)/(ν·kk j)` and\nthe two-source dissipation-scale condition\n`(1+γ)·max(β j, β(j+1)) ≤ θ·ν·kk j` (`θ ≤ 1`), the pairwise\nmaxima decay geometrically:\n`max (β (2m)) (β (2m+1)) ≤ θᵐ·max (β 0) (β 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium_two_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium_two_source","kind":"theorem","line":966,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L966-L988","doc":"Per-rung equilibrium with a second (nonlocal) source: forced by\n`Φ = kn·(P₁² + γ·P₂²)` and damped at `D = ν·kn²`, a rung starting\nempty never exceeds `(P₁² + γ·P₂²)/(ν·kn)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_tail_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_tail_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":908,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L908-L940","doc":"**Trajectory-level tail collapse**: adding the dissipation-scale\ncondition on the composed bounds (`rungBound n ≤ θ·ν·k (n+1)`,\nwith `θ ≥ 0` and `0 ≤ P`), the whole trajectory of rung `n` is\ngeometrically small: `u n t ≤ θⁿ·P`.  This closes the amplitude\nrepair's remainder (a) at the model level — the composition across\nrungs now holds along trajectories, not only at the bounds level. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qns-shell-tail-collapse","label":"prop:qns-shell-tail-collapse","md":"quantum-observable-universe/fluid-dynamics/qns-shell-tail-collapse.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_ladder_bounds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.trajectory_ladder_bounds","kind":"theorem","line":866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L866-L906","doc":"**Trajectory-level ladder composition**: for a rung family\n`u n t` (rung `n`, time `t`) with all tail rungs starting empty,\neach rung satisfying the per-amplitude DN step forced by the\n*actual trajectory* of the rung below, and the boundary rung\nuniformly bounded by `P`, every rung's whole trajectory obeys the\ncomposed bound: `u n t ≤ rungBound n`.  Rung-by-rung induction;\neach step is `rung_equilibrium` after upgrading the trajectory\nforcing to its constant bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rungBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rungBound","kind":"def","line":859,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L859-L864","doc":"The composed per-rung bounds: `rungBound 0 = P` (the boundary\ndatum), `rungBound (n+1) = (rungBound n)²/(ν·k (n+1))` (each rung\nat the equilibrium forced by the previous rung's bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.amplitude_ladder_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.amplitude_ladder_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":815,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L815-L842","doc":"**Geometric collapse of the amplitude ladder**: with the per-rung\nrecurrence `β(j+1) ≤ β(j)²/(ν·kk j)` (each rung's bound is the\nequilibrium forced by the previous) and the dissipation-scale\ncondition `β j ≤ θ·ν·kk j`, the bounds collapse geometrically:\n`β j ≤ θʲ·β 0`.  One induction; the doubly-exponential collapse\nthat actually occurs is stronger, but geometric suffices for the\n`ε`-uniform tail-enstrophy sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.rung_equilibrium","kind":"theorem","line":792,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L792-L813","doc":"**Per-rung equilibrium**: a rung starting empty, forced by the rung\nbelow (`Φ = kn·P²`) and damped at its own dissipation rate\n(`D = ν·kn²`), never exceeds the equilibrium `P²/(ν·kn)`.\n(`tail_damped_forced_bound` specialised to one scalar rung;\nthe DN per-amplitude step drops only a non-positive term.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.boundary_flux_tail_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.boundary_flux_tail_bound","kind":"theorem","line":729,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L729-L754","doc":"**The boundary-flux tail bound, in-model form**: with the\namplitude-forced step (the DN boundary structure) and the tail's\nown control of its boundary amplitude, the sup-in-time tail bound\nholds for all data with the explicit `ε`-uniform equilibrium\n`F²/(D²·kB2)`:\n\n  `Ω_tail(n) ≤ max(Ω_tail(0), F²/(D²·kB2))`.\n\n(Composition of the absorption with `tail_damped_forced_bound` at\n`Φ = F²/(2DkB2)`, damping `D/2`; the equilibrium is\n`Φ/(D/2) = F²/(D²kB2)`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.sqrt_forced_to_damped_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.sqrt_forced_to_damped_forced","kind":"theorem","line":694,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L694-L727","doc":"**Absorption of amplitude-proportional forcing** (AM-GM, no square\nroots): if the tail obeys the amplitude-forced step\n`Ωt(n+1) ≤ Ωt(n) + δ·(F·a(n) − D·Ωt(n))` with the tail controlling\nits own boundary amplitude (`kB2·a(n)² ≤ Ωt(n)`), then it obeys\nthe constant-forced step with `Φ = F²/(2·D·kB2)` and damping\n`D/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.tail_damped_forced_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.tail_damped_forced_bound","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L615-L662","doc":"**The damped-forced invariant**: if the tail obeys\n`Ωt(n+1) ≤ Ωt(n) + δ·(Φ − D·Ωt(n))` (uniform input `Φ`, damping\nrate `D`), with `0 ≤ δD ≤ 1`, `Φ ≥ 0`, `D > 0`, then\n\n  `Ωt(n) ≤ max(Ωt(0), Φ/D)`  for every `n`.\n\nBelow the equilibrium `Φ/D` the state may rise but never past the\nequilibrium; above it the drift is downward.  All constants are\nthose of the fixed band — `ε` does not appear. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.energy_geometric_decay","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.energy_geometric_decay","kind":"theorem","line":554,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L554-L580","doc":"**Geometric energy decay from the discrete Poincaré bound**: with\nthe dissipation step `E(n+1) ≤ E(n) − δν·Ω(n)`, the spectral-gap\nbound `g·E(n) ≤ Ω(n)` (with `g = k²ₘᵢₙ`), nonnegative energy, and\nthe step-size sanity `0 ≤ δν·g ≤ 1`, the energy decays\ngeometrically: `E_n ≤ (1 − δν·g)ⁿ·E₀`.  The rate `δν·g` carries\nthe `ε`-non-uniformity of the physical-layer infrared gap\n(`g = ε²`); see the section docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.energy_small_global","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.energy_small_global","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L494-L522","doc":"**Energy-small global regularity, fully composed — every link a\ntheorem.**  Hypotheses: the physical Leray dissipation step, the\ndamped quadratic low-mode step, good data (`Ωp 0 ≤ lam`), and the\ntwo arithmetic side conditions (`4E₀/δ ≤ Nbad·lam`, the bootstrap\nhorizon `H·δc·lam ≤ 1/4`, and the gap condition `Nbad + 1 ≤ H` —\njointly the `8cE₀ ≲ 1` energy-smallness reading).  Conclusion:\n`Ωp n ≤ 2·lam` for **every** `n`, uniformly in `ε`.  The only\nassumptions are the model's discrete dynamics and the smallness\narithmetic; no bootstrap, basin, or counting hypothesis remains\nundischarged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.hboot_of_local_bootstrap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.hboot_of_local_bootstrap","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L463-L492","doc":"**`hboot` discharged from GP3**: applying `local_bootstrap` to the\nsequence shifted to start at a good step `g` (the shift inherits\nthe quadratic step) gives the bootstrap cover\n`Ωp (g+j) ≤ 2·lam` for `j ≤ H`, under the horizon condition\n`H·(δc·lam) ≤ 1/4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.quadratic_step_of_damped","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.quadratic_step_of_damped","kind":"theorem","line":453,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L453-L461","doc":"The damped quadratic step implies GP3's undamped step: for\n`d, Ω ≥ 0`, `δ·Ω·(c·Ω − d) ≤ δ·c·Ω²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.sup_bound_of_chaining","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.sup_bound_of_chaining","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L374-L428","doc":"**Sup bound by good-step chaining**: if at most `Nbad` steps in any\nhorizon are bad (`lam < Ωp`), the origin is good (`Ωp 0 ≤ lam`),\nthe bootstrap covers `H` steps from every good step\n(`Ωp g ≤ lam → Ωp (g + j) ≤ 2·lam` for `j ≤ H`), and every bad run\nfits under the horizon (`Nbad + 1 ≤ H`), then `Ωp n ≤ 2·lam` for\n**every** `n`.  Latest-good-step pigeonhole: the newest good step\n`g ≤ n` is at most `Nbad` back, since the strictly-later steps up\nto `n` are all bad and there are at most `Nbad` of those in total;\nthe bootstrap from `g` then covers `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.bad_count_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.bad_count_le","kind":"theorem","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L353-L371","doc":"Convert the epochs product inequality into a natural-number bad\ncount: if `(4/δ)·E₀ ≤ Nbad·lam` (with `lam > 0`), then at most\n`Nbad` steps of any horizon are bad. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.eventual_regularity_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.eventual_regularity_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L302-L318","doc":"**Discrete eventual regularity, fully composed — no unproved\nhypothesis in the chain**: Leray hypotheses + the damped quadratic\nlow-mode step give a step `i₀ < m` (for any `m` with\n`(4/δ)·E₀ < m·(d/c)`) after which the enstrophy stays at or below\nthe threshold `d/c` forever.  Blow-up, if any, lives only inside\nthe ε-uniform initial window `[0, m)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.quadratic_basin_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.quadratic_basin_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L282-L300","doc":"**Basin invariance from the damped quadratic step** (GP4's\nmechanism, layer-agnostic): if\n`Ω(n+1) ≤ Ω(n) + δ·Ω(n)·(c·Ω(n) − d)` with `δ, Ω ≥ 0` and\n`c > 0`, then the sub-level set of `θ = d/c` is forward-invariant —\nbelow threshold the drift term is non-positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.eventually_in_basin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.eventually_in_basin","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L231-L259","doc":"**Discrete eventual regularity**: with the pigeonhole entry and a\nforward-invariant basin (`Ωp n ≤ θ → Ωp (n+1) ≤ θ`, the abstract\nshape of GP4's sub-threshold global persistence), there is a step\n`i₀ < m` from which the enstrophy stays `≤ θ` forever.  Blow-up,\nif any, is confined to the ε-uniformly bounded initial window\n`[0, m)` with any `m > 4E₀/(δθ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.exists_small_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.exists_small_step","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L202-L229","doc":"**Pigeonhole entry into any sub-level set, ε-uniform**: if\n`(4/δ)·E₀ < m·θ` then some step `i < m` has `Ωp i ≤ θ`.\n(Otherwise all `m` steps exceed `θ` and the cumulative bound is\nviolated.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.epochs_of_regularity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.epochs_of_regularity","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L132-L174","doc":"**Discrete epochs of regularity, ε-uniform**: under the physical\nLeray hypotheses, for every level `lam` the count of time steps\n`i < n` with `lam < tail i` satisfies the product inequality\n\n  `(card bad) · lam ≤ (4/δ)·E₀`,\n\nwith constants uniform in `ε`, `n`, and the data beyond `E₀`.\nWhen `0 < lam` this yields the count bound\n`card bad ≤ 4E₀/(δ·lam)` on dividing by `lam`; for `lam ≤ 0` the\ninequality is vacuously generous.  (Requires `0 ≤ tail` so that\noff-bad-set terms cannot hide negative mass.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.physical_tail_leray_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.physical_tail_leray_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L90-L111","doc":"**ε-uniform time-averaged tail bound** — the proved half of the\nphysical-layer no-pile-up hypothesis: any above-band tail sequence\n(`tail ≤ Ω_phys` pointwise in time) has `ε`-uniformly bounded\ncumulative sum, `(δ/4)·∑_{i<n} tail(i) ≤ E₀`.  The tail may spike\nat instants; its time integral cannot grow with `1/ε`.  The\nsup-in-time version is the open classical weak-vs-strong gap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.physical_leray_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.physical_leray_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L61-L88","doc":"**ε-uniform physical-layer Leray bound**: with the physical\ndissipation step `E(n+1) ≤ E(n) − δ·(1/(2q))·Ω_phys(n)` and\n`1 < q ≤ 2`, the cumulative physical enstrophy satisfies\n\n  `(δ/4)·∑_{i<n} Ω_phys(i) ≤ E₀`\n\nfor every `n` — all constants independent of `ε = q − 1`.  The\nfixed-`ν` frame's a-priori control survives the classical limit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.nu_phys_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.PhysicalLayerLeray.nu_phys_lower","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/physical_layer_leray.lean#L50-L59","doc":"The physical viscosity is uniformly bounded below on the substrate\nwindow: `1 < q ≤ 2` gives `1/4 ≤ 1/(2q)`.  (The whole campaign\nworks at `q = 1 + ε` with small `ε > 0`, so `q ≤ 2` is not a\nrestriction in practice; it is stated explicitly rather than\nhidden.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}